Proposal 0002: gate every paid AI workflow on autonomy/POLICY.yaml. NOT APPLIED.

PROTECTED: every file in this patch is a protected path (.github/workflows/**,
autonomy/**; T3 in autonomy/POLICY.yaml, two human approvals). Apply only after
a human edit or explicit owner approval of this protected-file change:

    git apply docs/proposals/0002-ai-workflow-gating.patch

What it does:
- knowledge-sync, learnings-triage, gardener (loop "loop-knowledge") and
  ai-review (new loop "loop-review") each get a `gate` job that runs
  scripts/ci/ai_gate.py from a trusted ref (main, or the PR's base commit
  for ai-review, so a PR cannot enable its own review) and exports
  run / max_turns / max_budget_usd / timeout_minutes.
- Every job with a Claude step `needs: gate`, runs only when run == 'true',
  takes timeout-minutes from the policy, and passes --max-turns and
  --max-budget-usd from the policy. claude-code-security-review has no turn
  or dollar input, so it is bounded by timeout only (claudecode-timeout).
- POLICY.yaml gains "loop-review", disabled with a zero budget, so the gate
  denies until a human sets real numbers.

Limits: --max-budget-usd is per run and is set to the loop's daily_usd;
nothing meters spend across runs in a day, and the global caps are not
enforced by this gate.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ai-review.yml b/.github/workflows/ai-review.yml
index 83be4f5..c242641 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ai-review.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ai-review.yml
@@ -17,10 +17,36 @@ concurrency:
   cancel-in-progress: true
 
 jobs:
+  # Reads autonomy/POLICY.yaml and scripts/ci/ai_gate.py from a trusted ref; the paid
+  # job below runs only on run=true, with the loop's turn, dollar and time budget.
+  gate:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
+    timeout-minutes: 5
+    permissions:
+      contents: read
+    outputs:
+      run: ${{ steps.gate.outputs.run }}
+      max_turns: ${{ steps.gate.outputs.max_turns }}
+      max_budget_usd: ${{ steps.gate.outputs.max_budget_usd }}
+      timeout_minutes: ${{ steps.gate.outputs.timeout_minutes }}
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1
+        with:
+          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}
+          persist-credentials: false
+          sparse-checkout: |
+            autonomy
+            scripts/ci
+      - id: gate
+        env:
+          AUTONOMY_ENABLED: ${{ vars.AUTONOMY_ENABLED }}
+        run: python3 scripts/ci/ai_gate.py loop-review || echo "::notice::paid step skipped by ai_gate.py"
+
   security-review:
-    if: github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository && !github.event.pull_request.draft
+    needs: gate
+    if: needs.gate.outputs.run == 'true' && github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository && !github.event.pull_request.draft
     runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
-    timeout-minutes: 30
+    timeout-minutes: ${{ fromJSON(needs.gate.outputs.timeout_minutes) }}
     permissions:
       contents: read
       pull-requests: write # post review comments
@@ -51,11 +77,14 @@ jobs:
           claude-api-key: ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}
           comment-pr: true
           custom-security-scan-instructions: ${{ steps.prompt.outputs.path }}
+          # This action takes no turn or dollar cap; the job timeout and this are its only bounds.
+          claudecode-timeout: ${{ needs.gate.outputs.timeout_minutes }}
 
   code-review:
-    if: github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository && !github.event.pull_request.draft
+    needs: gate
+    if: needs.gate.outputs.run == 'true' && github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository && !github.event.pull_request.draft
     runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
-    timeout-minutes: 30
+    timeout-minutes: ${{ fromJSON(needs.gate.outputs.timeout_minutes) }}
     permissions:
       contents: read
       pull-requests: write # post review comments
@@ -102,4 +131,6 @@ jobs:
           github_token: ${{ github.token }}
           prompt: ${{ steps.prompt.outputs.text }}
           claude_args: |
+            --max-turns ${{ needs.gate.outputs.max_turns }}
+            --max-budget-usd ${{ needs.gate.outputs.max_budget_usd }}
             --allowedTools "mcp__github_inline_comment__create_inline_comment,Bash(gh pr comment:*),Bash(gh pr diff:*),Bash(gh pr view:*),Read,Grep,Glob"
